From a1a4c6530c6c67b5b5793a7a1c0fb031e40d46ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roger Luethi <luethi@osism.tech>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 21:35:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Do not cache angular templates inside compress

With offline compression, django-compressor names each compressed
block after a hash of the block's rendered content, both when
"manage.py compress" writes the manifest and when a request looks the
block up. The angular template preloads block wraps its content in a
{% cache %} fragment, so that content, and the key, come from whatever
the Django cache holds, not from the installed templates.

Deployments commonly share one cache backend between all dashboard
hosts, and the fragment outlives an upgrade (NG_TEMPLATE_CACHE_AGE).
After an image change, compress on a new host can hash the previous
release's fragment and write a manifest without the key for the new
templates. Once the fragment is replaced in the shared cache, requests
on that host fail with OfflineGenerationError ("key ... is missing
from offline manifest"). update_angular_template_hash only clears the
fragment after a block has been compressed, and only for the theme
being compressed, so it cannot prevent this. During a rolling upgrade
old hosts keep writing their fragment back, so clearing the cache
before compress does not prevent it either.

Render the angular templates directly inside the compress block. The
key then depends only on the installed templates. The cost is
rendering the templates on every request in offline mode instead of
reading the cached fragment.
---
 openstack_dashboard/templates/horizon/_scripts.html | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/openstack_dashboard/templates/horizon/_scripts.html b/openstack_dashboard/templates/horizon/_scripts.html
index d857fcd6..0c1600f8 100644
--- a/openstack_dashboard/templates/horizon/_scripts.html
+++ b/openstack_dashboard/templates/horizon/_scripts.html
@@ -63,9 +63,7 @@
 {% endcompress %}
 
 {% compress js file angular_template_cache_preloads %}
-  {% cache NG_TEMPLATE_CACHE_AGE angular 'template_cache_preloads' THEME %}
     {% angular_templates %}
-  {% endcache %}
 {% endcompress %}
 
 {% if profiler_enabled %}
